        "short_description": {
            "database_value": "Nouvelair Tunisie is a privately owned airline based in Tunisia, established in 1989 and known for its tourist charter flights. The airline operates primarily from Monastir Habib Bourguiba International Airport, with additional bases at Tunis–Carthage International Airport and Djerba–Zarzis International Airport. It specializes in connecting various European cities to popular Tunisian holiday resorts, making it a key player in the country's travel services.\n\nThe airline operates a modern fleet consisting entirely of Airbus A320-200 aircraft, ensuring efficiency for its charter services. Nouvelair is committed to providing affordable flights for leisure travelers, focusing on enhancing the tourism experience in Tunisia. The company is led by CEO Chokri Zarrad and is part of the Tunisian Travel Service group, which holds a majority stake in the airline.",
